  "body": "On current main (a3232e3e), with no local changes:\n\n    go test -tags nogui -race -count=2 ./internal/pii/\n\nis red with DATA RACE warnings (6 warnings across 2 runs on a WSL2 box,\ngo1.27.3). The writer is one test's cleanup restoring the package vars\n(fakeInstall.func2 at internal/pii/main_test.go:145, oldInstall.func1 at\ninternal/pii/fetch_test.go:226), the reader is an upgrade() goroutine\nthat outlived its test (binDir -> tagDir at internal/pii/pii.go:75,89),\nstarted by `go upgrade()` in start (internal/pii/serve.go). The goroutine\nis unowned: nothing waits for it, so it reads dir/serveTag/oldTags while\nthe next test's cleanup writes them back. The existing upgrade tests\ndodge it only by polling `upgrading` before they end, and a slow\nclassification (the slow fake) widens the window.\n\nReproduced on a clean worktree of a3232e3e; also seen at a rebased head\nwith an unrelated slow-classification test added, which is what surfaced\nit.",
