   "body": "Patch: https://github.com/JoeyWu-tech/magpie/tree/fix/3628-pii-upgrade-joined\n\ncommit 8b61a25d on origin/main 42ec2700 (applies as is on c158b043, pii hasn't changed since), `git format-patch --no-signature --full-index --stdout 42ec2700..8b61a25d | sha256sum` is `a972fd96d1f9b43cb4fb2e03e2f5adafd2798ff560290d282035ab2ec8cb266b`.\n\nstart runs upgrade through a WaitGroup (`upgrades`), and fakeInstall waits on it before it sets dir and in its cleanup, after Stop. Your command (`-race -count=2`) is ok with 0 warnings, and so is `-count=10`. To make it bite harder I also delayed upgrade 0 to 200ms at its top (not committed): main gets 8 warnings with `-count=3`, this gets 0, with `-shuffle=on` too. The body has the hand-breaks.\n\n@skygunner I ran 80cea91a under the same delay too, since it waits in the same two places. It was red in 1 of 2 runs (TestServeStartsWithoutResidencyHeartbeat), and on the three tests that start pf-serve twice it caught TestGPUDeathMovesToCPU on the first try:\n\n```\nWrite at 0x000000e80858 by goroutine 169:\n  pii.fakeInstall.func2()  main_test.go:137\nPrevious read at 0x000000e80858 by goroutine 175:\n  pii.tagDir()  pii.go:73\n  pii.binDir()  pii.go:88\n  pii.upgrade()  fetch.go:167\nGoroutine 175 (finished) created at:\n  pii.goUpgrade()  fetch.go:146\n  pii.start()  serve.go:83\n  ...\n  pii.TestGPUDeathMovesToCPU()  serve_test.go:82\n```\n\nThat upgrade is the first start's, on the GPU. `upgradeDone` keeps only the last upgrade's channel, so `waitUpgrade` never joins it. A WaitGroup joins every upgrade a test began, which is the only real difference between the two. Which one goes in is yetone's call.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
