   "updated_at": "2026-10-25T18:20:46Z",
   "body": "The goroutine is owned now, on [fix/pii-upgrade-race](https://github.com/skygunner/magpie/tree/fix/pii-upgrade-race) (`80cea91a`, based on today's `main`):\n\n- `goUpgrade` hands `go upgrade()` a done channel (`upgradeDone`, the last started's), and `waitUpgrade` waits for the one under way — at once when none is.\n- `fakeInstall` and `oldInstall` call `waitUpgrade` before their package vars move — at cleanup, as your trace shows, and at setup too: `TestWarm`'s second `fakeInstall` writes `dir` while the first `Warm`'s upgrade still reads it, which is the same race one test earlier than the cleanup.\n\nYour command is green here now:\n\n```\ngo test -tags nogui -race -count=2 ./internal/pii/   # ok, 32s\ngo test -tags nogui -race -count=3 ./internal/pii/   # ok\n```\n\nBefore the fix that same run was red on this box too (three DATA RACE warnings, `TestOldServeRunsUntilUpgraded` and `TestWarm` failing, go1.26.8). The `upgrading` polls the upgrade tests used as their dodge are left as they were — the wait makes them safe without changing what they wait for. Plain `-count=1` suites and vet on linux and windows are clean.\n",
   "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
